@startuml sequence-1-game
!include style.iuml
title Restaurant Rush | One choice-sensitive game (sequence 1 of 4)
caption Same base configuration, arrival schedule and meal rules; only manager choices differ.
actor Manager
boundary "ui : ConsoleUI" as UI
participant "CommandParser\n(static)" as Parser
control "controller : TurnController" as TC
autonumber

note over Manager, TC
  Fixtures: stage-3/host-combo-happy-hour and stage-3/defeat.
  GameSetup.baseGame() wires Host, two tables, 18 turns and mixed arrivals.
  Pages 2-4 expand the winning run's C3/O3 interactions; other customers
  use the same methods. Loop guards and labels summarize Java conditions.
end note

alt manager follows host-combo-happy-hour.in
  loop !controller.isOver(); turns 1 through 18
    UI -> TC : snapshot()
    TC --> UI : Snapshot (availability is controller-owned)
    opt snapshot.happyHourAvailable()
      UI --> Manager : Manager> (HAPPY_HOUR or SKIP)
      Manager -> UI : SKIP on turns 1-6; HAPPY_HOUR on turn 7
      UI -> Parser : parseHappyHour(line)
      Parser --> UI : Optional<Boolean>
      note right of Parser
        Invalid manager input is retried
        before beginTurn; no turn consumed.
      end note
    end
    UI -> TC : beginTurn(activateHappyHour)
    ref over UI, TC : Page 2: turn-7 activation, arrival and Host seating
    TC --> UI : TurnStart(events, snapshot)
    UI --> Manager : render events, state and remaining duration
    loop controller.currentRole().isPresent(); Host then Waiter then Chef
      UI -> TC : snapshot()
      TC --> UI : Snapshot with current role's legalActions
      UI --> Manager : numbered legal actions and role prompt
      Manager -> UI : number or text command from fixture
      UI -> Parser : parse(line, role, legalActions)
      Parser --> UI : Optional<Action>
      alt parse returned empty
        UI -> Parser : errorFor(line, role, legalActions)
        Parser --> UI : error text
        UI --> Manager : error; retry same role
      else parsed Action
        UI -> TC : submit(action)
        ref over UI, TC : Pages 2-4: real staff/domain calls for C3 and O3
        TC --> UI : ActionResult
        alt rejected
          UI --> Manager : reason; retry same role (no mutation)
        else accepted, including WAIT
          UI --> Manager : events, or message when no events
          note right of TC : Accepted action advances one phase.
        end
      end
    end
    UI -> TC : endTurn()
    ref over UI, TC : Page 4: eating, automatic payment, waiting loss, result
    TC --> UI : TurnEnd(events, summary, optional result)
    UI --> Manager : end-of-turn summary; final result on turn 18
  end
  note over Manager, TC #E5F2E9
    VICTORY: five payments, 7494 cents, satisfactionSum 419, average 83.8.
    All targets hold: paidCount >= 4, revenueCents >= 4500,
    satisfactionSum >= 60 * paidCount (419 >= 300).
    Payments: C1@4 900/92; C2@7 1350/95; C3@12 1944/84;
    C4@15 1800/64; C5@17 1500/84 (cents/satisfaction).
  end note
else manager follows defeat.in: every opportunity is skipped/waited
  loop turns 1 through 18
    UI --> Manager : Manager>
    Manager -> UI : SKIP
    UI -> Parser : parseHappyHour("SKIP")
    Parser --> UI : Optional.of(false)
    UI -> TC : beginTurn(false)
    TC --> UI : arrivals/state; Happy Hour remains unused
    loop Host then Waiter then Chef
      Manager -> UI : WAIT
      UI -> Parser : parse("WAIT", role, legalActions)
      Parser --> UI : Action(role, WAIT, null)
      UI -> TC : submit(action)
      TC --> UI : accepted; phase advances; no staff operation
    end
    UI -> TC : endTurn()
    TC --> UI : waiting loss; C1 leaves on 13, C4 on 18; summary/result
  end
  note over Manager, TC #FBEAE6
    DEFEAT: paidCount 0, revenue 0, satisfactionSum 0, leftCount 2; average N/A.
    No seats, orders or payments. C2/C3/C5/C6 remain WAITING at 25/4/52/76.
    No early ending: both branches complete all 18 turns.
  end note
end

legend bottom left
  Solid message arrows are calls/input; dashed arrows are returns/output.
  ref frames expand into pages 2-4, not additional Java methods.
  Role/phase retries do not add a turn or consume a successful staff action.
endlegend
footer Checked against merged Stage 3 code d38231a and the two unchanged Stage 3 fixtures.
@enduml
